      "text": "To find the probability that both chosen members are girls, we need to consider the total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10 and the number of favorable outcomes (choosing 2 girls).\n\nTotal number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10 = $\\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = 45$\n\nNumber of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5 = $\\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = 10$\n\nProbability that both chosen members are girls = (Number of ways to choose 2 girls) / (Total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10) = 10 / 45 = 2 / 9",
